Once these machines of war had enthralled their beholders;
now they were lifeless and oddly beautiful as they threw long shad-
ows across the desert from the late autumn sun settling in the west.

No doubt the Russians would take
all eastern Germany and the Balkans, and the British and Ameri-
cans everything west of that line;

Lee had put
together a special train of a dozen coaches for his journeys around
England;

Some of the wounded had scooped out shallow trenches
to escape the artillery falling at ten-second intervals along the beach;
those who then died rested in graves they had dug for themselves.

Hughes
and Patton dined together, then Patton invited him to stay for the
night and gave him a sleeping bag;

He boast-
ed to Lee that all Eisenhower had to do was change the boundary;
then he could push on north and take Falaise himself.

He spent the next day
working on a report to the Combined Chiefs of Staﬀ on Nazi losses
and reviewing with General Betts the usual dossiers;

But the whole
Allied team rallied to meet the danger; national considerations were
thrown overboard;

Big John
Littl e john, of whom Eisenhower was especially fond, travelled in
a special train, with morning newspapers delivered at every stop;
